  "summary": "Take part in a polite class debate: give arguments for and against an idea, link them with مِنْ نَاحِيَةٍ… وَمِنْ نَاحِيَةٍ أُخْرَى، لٰكِنَّ، مَعَ أَنَّ، بِالْإِضَافَةِ إِلَى and لِذٰلِكَ, and agree or disagree with أُوَافِقُ and لَا أُوَافِقُ.",
  "intro": "A debate, نِقَاش, needs more than opinions: you need linking words to build an argument. Weigh two sides with مِنْ نَاحِيَةٍ… وَمِنْ نَاحِيَةٍ أُخْرَى (on the one hand… on the other hand). Add a point with بِالْإِضَافَةِ إِلَى (in addition to), give a result with لِذٰلِكَ (that's why, so), and turn the argument with لٰكِنَّ (but) or مَعَ أَنَّ (although). Like أَنَّ, these two put the next noun in -a or take a pronoun ending: لٰكِنَّهُ (but it), مَعَ أَنَّهُ (although it). To stay polite, start with مَعَ احْتِرَامِي (with respect) before لَا أُوَافِقُ (I don't agree).",
